\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar Closes Slightly Higher, Down Sharply for Week \b0\par\par\uc2 887 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Mai 2003\par 01:20\par \uc2  Dow Jones Business News \par \uc2 DJON\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2003, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dow Jones Newswires\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The dollar took a pause in its downward trek Friday, finishing the day\par little changed against its major rivals but down sharply since Monday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  After a steep decline earlier in the week, the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  managed to halt its slide at least temporarily as traders booked profits and adjusted positions ahead of a long weekend for the London and Tokyo markets. \par \par \uc2  "It was largely technical trading in a thin market," said David Leaver, senior trader at Gain Capital. \par \par \uc2  The dollar garnered some support from the U.S. employment report for April and the subsequent rally for U.S. equities, while unimpressive economic data from Europe tarnished the euro and worries over Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  capped the yen, traders said. \par \par \uc2  However, the underlying trend remains bearish for the dollar, with the euro remaining at four-year highs versus its U.S. counterpart. The common European \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is still in demand, said Mr. Leaver, especially from accounts based outside the U.S. \par \par \uc2  The April employment report proved to be better than some had feared, but didn't really give the market much reason to cheer once the figures had been analyzed, according to traders. \par \par \uc2  The payroll decline in April was less than economists had expected after two months of steep cuts, but the nation's unemployment rate moved higher as U.S. employers cut jobs for a third-consecutive month, suggesting the overall economy continues to struggle. The unemployment rate rose to 6% from 5.8% in March, the Labor Department said. \par \par \uc2  The April figures aren't "going to change people's attitude about the economy," said Marc Chandler, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at HSBC in New York, noting the data could "further embolden" dollar bears next week. \par \par \uc2  Later in the morning, U.S. factory orders for March came in above expectations and U.S. equities pushed firmly into positive territory, with the Dow Jones Industrial Average ending up 1.5% and the Nasdaq Composite Index advancing 2.1%. \par \par \uc2  Late Friday in New York, the euro was trading at $1.1224, down from $1.1239 late Thursday in New York but up sharply from $1.0987 late Monday. After falling as far as 118.42 yen earlier in the day, the dollar rebounded to 118.95 yen from 118.55 yen late Thursday, but still under 120.41 yen from Monday. \par \par \uc2  Japanese officials had warned about excessive yen strength during the Asian session. Around midday in New York, a report from Japan's JiJi Press indicated Japan's three-party ruling bloc will call for flexible yen-weakening market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  as part of its emergency economic proposals to be compiled early next week. \par \par \uc2  Citing unnamed sources, JiJi said the Liberal Democratic Party, the New Komeito and the New Conservative Party will ask monetary authorities to step into \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets in an appropriate manner to stem any excessive rise in the yen. \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's government has a long history of using \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the markets to stop the yen from reaching levels it feels will hurt the competitiveness of Japanese products in the world markets. \par \par \uc2  The pound fell back to $1.6045 from $1.6100 late Thursday, but is up from $1.5892 Monday in New York. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, Mexico's peso moved to its strongest level since late last year, as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  began the first of its planned dollar auctions aimed at slowing the accumulation of reserves. \par \par \uc2  On 48-hour spot dollar markets in Mexico City, Banamex quoted the peso closing at a midrate of 10.20 Mexican pesos to the dollar on a spread of 10.19 to 10.21 Mexican pesos. That compared with 10.2650 Mexican pesos at the opening. \par \par \uc2  It was the peso's strongest close since Dec. 23, as the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  continued to rally on the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sales. The peso's burst of strength came as somewhat of a surprise. The auctions, which will exceed $2 billion over a three-month period, were widely thought to have been priced in as the peso recovered from its record low close of 11.2220 Mexican pesos on March 5. \par \par \uc2  Farther afield, the South African rand weakened sharply against the dollar late Friday on selling attributed to a report by the International Monetary Fund on Wednesday, saying the fund didn't see much scope for further gains. South African and Mexican financial markets were closed Thursday for a public holiday. \par \par \uc2  Late in New York, the rand was at 7.4750 rand against the dollar, sharply lower than 7.2650 rand late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  El Tigani Ibrahim, the IMF's representative in South Africa, said it was impossible to predict the timing of a turnaround for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but said he expected to see the rand sliding back to 8.400 rand to the dollar. The rand hit a 31-month high at 7.0450 rand earlier in the week but failed to break the crucial technical barrier at seven rand, even though local chartists were touting a move to 6.8500 rand. \par \par \uc2  Write to Robert Flint at robert.flint@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  (Anthony Harrup in Mexico City and Adam Aljewicz in Johannesburg contributed to this report) \par \par \uc2  Copyright (c) 2003 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2  All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires \par \par \uc2  05-02-03 1920ET \par \par \uc2 Dokument djon000020030502dz5200795\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
