\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar shunted to 4 year low on weak US data. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Daniel Bases \par \uc2 746 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Mai 2003\par 22:41\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  NEW YORK, May 1 (Reuters) - Weak U.S. manufacturing and jobs data shunted the dollar to a fresh four-year low against the euro on Thursday as investors' sense of gloom surrounding the world's biggest economy deepened. \par \par \uc2  The Institute for Supply Management's gauge of U.S. manufacturing contracted for a second straight month while weekly jobless data remained stubbornly high and productivity grew less than expected. \par \par \uc2  While the sluggish U.S. economy is still stronger than the majority of the rest of the world, investors have witnessed a week's worth of disappointing data. \par \par \uc2  But the gloom surrounding the dollar could turn out to have a silver lining on Friday after the hotly anticipated April employment report is released. \par \par \uc2  "Everyone has been positioning against the dollar all week because they think the employment report is going to be bad. If that turns out true then it becomes a classic 'sell the rumor buy the fact,' ie: buy the dollar back," said Ralph DelZenero, managing director of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  at Bank One in Chicago. \par \par \uc2  Economists expect April's unemployment rate to rise to 5.9 percent from 5.8 percent and the loss of 53,000 non-farm jobs. \par \par \uc2  "We are seeing the path of least resistance right now in the euro's rise, but it might be time to buy the dollar back because all the bad news will be behind us," he said. \par \par \uc2  The euro shot up to a new four-year high for the second consecutive day, hitting $1.1287, before slipping back to $1.1237, still a gain of 0.50 percent compared with Wednesday's New York close. \par \par \uc2  "Every day you hear talking heads going on about how high the euro is going from here. Everybody is bullish the euro, which usually is not a good sign," said Mike Malpede, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst at Refco Group in Chicago. \par \par \uc2  The dollar slumped to a near one-month low against the yen, trading down to 118.18 yen, before cutting its losses to trade at 118.54 yen, a loss of 0.25 percent on the day. \par \par \uc2  But the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's recent gains against the dollar have raised nervousness that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  again to stem the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's export-damaging strength. \par \par \uc2  In the first quarter the BOJ admitted that it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market and talk of new interest put investors on guard. \par \par \uc2  Japan's top financial diplomat, Zembei Mizoguchi, said on Thursday that authorities were watching the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market carefully and would take action if needed. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Japan, which acts on behalf of Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the event of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , did not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in April, according to official data. \par \par \uc2  Several trading sources said the dollar found some support after rumors circulated in the market that the Bank of Japan was calling into the market for prices and interested in the 118 yen level. \par \par \uc2  The dollar tumbled to a five-year low against the Canadian dollar as weak U.S. economic data is negatively contrasted against strong Canadian results and the lifting of the SARS-induced ban on travel to Toronto. \par \par \uc2  The greenback fell to a low of C$1.4164 against the loonie, before cutting the loss to C$1.4186, still down 1 percent on the day. Canada's high benchmark interest rates and indications from the Bank of Canada that it could hike rates even further only added to the selling pressure against the greenback. \par \par \uc2  SPECULATION ABOUT POOR JOBS DATA \par \par \uc2  "What we are seeing is speculative trading ahead of the expected poor April U.S. employment report tomorrow. Because the report is expected to show continued weakness in the U.S. economy, this is going to be a dollar negative," said Michael Woolfolk, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist with The Bank of New York. \par \par \uc2  Data ahead of the jobs report was not inspiring. \par \par \uc2  On Thursday, the ISM reported its manufacturing index fell to 45.4 in April from 46.2 in March. Economists expected a reading of 47.3. A reading below 50 signals contraction. \par \par \uc2  U.S. weekly initial jobless claims and productivity data dealt the greenback a muted blow. Claims fell to 448,000 in the week to April 26, but were higher than expected. Productivity rose 1.6 percent in the first quarter, slower than the expected 2.1 percent. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030501dz5100zyv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
