\par\par \b \uc2  UPDATE 1-Japan stepped up yen-selling campaign in March. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Mariko Hayashibara \par \uc2 567 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2003\par 13:02\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, March 31 (Reuters) - Japan said on Monday that it stepped up its efforts to prevent an export-crimping rise in the yen over the past month, buying 1.2 trillion yen worth of dollars and euros in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , conducted from late February to early March, brings cumulative yen-selling by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MOF) to around 2.4 trillion yen after about 510 billion yen in February and 680 billion yen in January. \par \par \uc2  "\b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was conducted over several occasions from late February to early March," a senior ministry official told reporters. \par \par \uc2  The ministry said Japan acted alone and that the aim was to control volatility in the market, which had been gyrating on concerns about the U.S.-led war in Iraq. \par \par \uc2  "To avoid risks of a 'March crisis' and ill effects from war in Iraq, Japanese monetary authorities seemed to have tried hard to halt the yen's rise," said Tomoko Fujii, director and economist at Nikko Salomon Smith Barney. \par \par \uc2  "I think the MOF wants to stress that the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was a cooperative action with the BOJ (Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 ), which has injected massive amount of funds into the market toward the end of this month," she said. \par \par \uc2  Koji Fukaya, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst at Bank of Tokyo-Mitsubishi, said Japan most likely spent about 500 to 700 billion yen in the last two days of February alone. \par \par \uc2  "In late February, the yen was already at a high level and the dollar's outlook was increasingly weak due to Iraq jitters, so authorities seemed to have wanted to take pre-emptive action," he said. \par \par \uc2  EYEING YEAR-END \par \par \uc2  Speculation in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  was conducting "stealth" \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  helped underpin the dollar against the yen over the past month. \par \par \uc2  The authorities were expected to try to keep the dollar above 120 yen ahead of the March 31 annual bookclosings for most Japanese companies. \par \par \uc2  Having appreciated as high as 116.36 yen in early March, the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell as low as 121.88 yen on March 21. \par \par \uc2  But the dollar retreated below 119 yen on Monday as worries grew that the war in Iraq could last longer than expected and weigh on an already weak U.S. economy. \par \par \uc2  As the dollar looks set to remain under pressure, analysts expect \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  will keep \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  "I expect factors unfavourable to the dollar would continue to emerge, and the dollar could fall towards 116 yen over around a one-month period," said Bank of Tokyo-Mitsubishi's Fukaya. \par \par \uc2  Japan has been selling its own \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  intermittently since 1999 and the latest \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  will increase Japanese external reserves, which were already at a record high of $485.265 billion at the end of February, more than twice as high as in January 1999. \par \par \uc2  Between April and June last year, \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  spent a record amount on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , forking out 4.0162 trillion yen to sap the yen's strength. \par \par \uc2  "Considering Japan's economic conditions, I don't think the authorities will change their stance to stop the yen strengthening beyond 115 yen," said Yasunari Ueno, chief market economist at Mizuho Securities. \par \par \uc2  "There's a tacit understanding among G7 nations to prevent a rapid dollar fall due to the Iraq war." \par \par \uc2  ($1=119.75 Yen). \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030331dz3v00lxe\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
