\par\par \b \uc2  BOJ data show Japan sold yen in  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  market in March. \b0\par\par\uc2 262 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2003\par 12:24\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, March 31 (Reuters) - Japanese monetary authorities conducted yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the third straight month in March, buying 1.131 trillion yen ($9.44 billion) worth of other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market, Bank of Japan data showed on Monday. \par \par \uc2  The figures suggest that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MOF), worried about an export-crimping rise in the yen, stepped up its discreet "stealth" \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  as the market gyrated on concerns about the U.S.-led war in Iraq. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ data showed that the MOF paid the amount to the private sector through its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  account, which mostly represents \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The figure included the last two business days in February as transactions on those days were settled in March. Most market-watchers believe that Japanese authorities \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on those two days. \par \par \uc2  The March figure brings cumulative yen selling by the MOF to 2.32 trillion yen after 513 billion yen in February and 678 billion yen in January. \par \par \uc2  As the fiscal year in Japan drew to a close, speculation grew in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  had been conducting "stealth" \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to make sure the dollar held above 120 yen on Monday, when many of the country's companies closed their books for the financial year. \par \par \uc2  But the greenback slumped to a two-week low around 119 yen in Asian trade on Monday on rising worries that the war in Iraq could last longer than expected and weigh on an already weak U.S. economy. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030331dz3v00kzo\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
