\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar Gains Against Rivals in Muddy Session \b0\par\par\uc2 789 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2003\par 01:04\par \uc2  Dow Jones Business News \par \uc2 DJON\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2003, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dow Jones Newswires\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The dollar ended mostly higher Tuesday after hitting fresh four-year\par lows against the euro, as confusion surrounding the outcome of a United\par Nations vote on a second resolution complicated market direction.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  Ongoing speculation the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  may be covertly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the yen contributed to choppy trading, helping the dollar rebound and move back above the key psychological level of 117 yen. \par \par \uc2  In late dealings Tuesday, the dollar was at 117.07 yen, down from a session high of 117.29 yen but up from 116.83 yen in late New York trading Monday. The euro was at $1.1039, down from its four-year high of $1.1084 and from $1.1055 late Monday in New York. Sterling was at $1.6069, compared with $1.6021 late Monday in New York. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the dollar's gains didn't carry much conviction. \par \par \uc2  "There are no fundamentals that explain these movements," said Ashraf Laidi, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at MG Financial in New York. "It does not take away from the general negative tone of the dollar in light of the uncertainty in the Security Council. \par \par \uc2  In a day of heightened diplomatic shuffling, the Bush administration said it expects the U.N. Security Council to vote on a second resolution drafted by the U.S., United Kingdom and Spain sometime this week, despite threats by France and Russia to veto any such action. \par \par \uc2  Although some Security Council members have called on the U.S. and its allies to extend the deadline for Iraq to destroy its weapons of mass destruction, White House spokesman Ari Fleischer said the U.S. is willing to tweak the resolution but not extend the deadline by a month or a month-and-a-half. \par \par \uc2  Muddying the picture further, France said it is "open to dialogue" to solve the impasse at the U.N. but won't budge on the fundamentals it has championed since the start of the Iraqi crisis. \par \par \uc2  Further clouding the uncertainty that is also weighing on the dollar, the six "undecided" members of the U.N. Security Council want to give Iraq a 45-day ultimatum to fully comply with U.N. disarmament demands or face a military attack. \par \par \uc2  Speculation the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  may have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the yen also supported the dollar in a number of instances during the global day, starting after remarks from a top Japanese financial official. \par \par \uc2  "If there are sudden rises or falls [in the yen], we must be ready to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  immediately," Finance Minister Masajuro Shiokawa told a press conference. The remarks followed reports Monday the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  stands ready to sell up to one trillion yen daily in order to weaken the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  ahead of fiscal year end. \par \par \uc2  A sharp dollar rally in midmorning trading gathered momentum on the back of what some traders believed was covert \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 . "It makes sense to assume there was \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Mr. Laidi, adding he reckons the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  wants the dollar above 117 yen. \par \par \uc2  In other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the Mexican peso closed stronger against the dollar for the fourth session in a row, recovering significant ground as investors continued to unload long dollar positions amid active trading. \par \par \uc2  Late in New York trade, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was quoted at 10.9125 Mexican pesos to the dollar, sharply stronger than 11.07 pesos late Monday. \par \par \uc2  The government's announcement that it plans to exchange some of its oil-related dollars in the open market has strengthened the Mexican \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to levels not seen since Feb. 24. Since then, the peso had been trading above the key 11-pesos-per-dollar mark, pressured by continued geopolitical jitters and a stronger euro. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, the Canadian dollar eased off its recent record highs, but analysts said the risk of a dramatic near-term weakening remains low and several factors suggest it will continue its rally. \par \par \uc2  The sheer magnitude of the Canadian dollar's 6.4% climb against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  this year has made some analysts cautious about the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's continued progress. One major concern for some market watchers is that speculative players' exposure to the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is hovering near record highs, a situation some argue makes the Canadian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  vulnerable to a sharp reversal. \par \par \uc2  However, others are convinced persistently strong fundamentals will allow the Canadian dollar to outperform its U.S. counterpart in the longer run. \par \par \uc2  Write to Agnes T. Crane at agnes.crane@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  (Santiago Perez in Mexico City and Don Curren in Toronto contributed to this report) \par \par \uc2  Copyright (c) 2003 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2  All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires \par \par \uc2  03-11-03 1904ET \par \par \uc2 Dokument djon000020030312dz3c00001\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
