\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar ticks up on caution over yen  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2  By Kazunori Takada \par \uc2 563 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2003\par 08:07\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, March 11 (Reuters) - The dollar squeezed out gains against the yen and the euro in Tokyo trade on Tuesday as wariness that Japan may step up its campaign to halt the yen's rise helped fend off Iraqi war fears. \par \par \uc2  The Nihon Keizai Shimbun business daily reported the government and the Bank of Japan (BOJ) were prepared to introduce measures to steady the domestic stock market. \par \par \uc2  The report said the Finance Ministry was considering massive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  of about 1.0 trillion yen ($8.56 billion). \par \par \uc2  That would would be substantially bigger than \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's total \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  so far this year, which Traders estimate at one to two trillion yen. \par \par \uc2  "I think there is a possibility that the government and the BOJ will draw up a package that will include (\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in) the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market," said Motoshi Imura, senior manager of the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  and treasury division at Bank of Tokyo-Mitsubishi. \par \par \uc2  "But I think many are still concerned whether such a \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy would be accepted by other nations." \par \par \uc2  Japanese officials worry that excessive strength in the yen could hurt exports, seen as the main support for a faltering economic recovery. \par \par \uc2  As of 0639 GMT, the dollar was at 117.13 yen compared with 116.79 in late New York. \par \par \uc2  The euro also eased slightly to $1.1025 compared with $1.1055 in late U.S. trade. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the market was starting to unwind dollar-short positions after seeing little movement on Monday and Tuesday, but they expect the dollar-buying to be short-lived. \par \par \uc2  The euro was flat versus the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at 129.05 yen \par \par \uc2  The Nikkei share average closed below the 8,000 mark for the first time in 20 years on Tuesday - just three weeks before the end-March book-closing for most Japanese companies. It ended down 2.24 percent at 7,862.43. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ said it bought an extra one trillion yen ($8.56 billion) in short-term bills earlier in the day, aimed at stemming recent stock market falls and preventing war worries from destabilising the money market. \par \par \uc2  DOLLAR STILL BEARISH \par \par \uc2  Still, most players are pessimistic about the greenback's outlook as expectations mount that Washington will soon wage war on Iraq and on concerns - sparked by poor U.S. job data last week - that continued U.S. economic growth is far from guaranteed even if a war ends quickly. \par \par \uc2  "We recently revised down our forecasts for the U.S. economy. There are growing worries over the U.S. economy not just because of Iraq," said Minori Takeuchi, vice president of research at J.P. Morgan Chase. \par \par \uc2  "I think it's quite possible the market will test the determination of Japanese authorities," he said. \par \par \uc2  When asked about the possibility of massive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Finance Minister Masajuro Shiokawa said on Tuesday that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  immediately if it sees undesirable volatility in exchange rates. \par \par \uc2  Whether massive or not, traders think \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  could \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  any time the dollar hovers below 117 yen, with 115 yen seen as the most important level for Japan to protect. \par \par \uc2  "I think it's pretty clear to anyone who has seen a dollar/yen chart that the dollar could dive once it breaks below 115 yen," said Kota Kimura, assistant manager at Shinkin \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . ($1=116.88 yen). \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030312dz3b00cck\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
