\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar steadied by Japan  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  threat but war fears loom. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Natsuko Waki \par \uc2 731 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2003\par 12:16\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, March 11 (Reuters) - The dollar held above last week's seven-month low against the yen on Tuesday following a report \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  might conduct massive yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  but an upcoming UN debate on disarming Iraq kept it on the defensive. \par \par \uc2  The Nihon Keizai Shimbun business daily reported Tokyo was prepared to steady the domestic stock market by introducing measures that could include further monetary easing and yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  of about 1.0 trillion yen a day. \par \par \uc2  News that Washington and London have been forced to delay a U.N. vote on their resolution giving Iraq a March 17 ultimatum to disarm or face war also lessened prospects for an immediate war, although many still see a U.S.-led war as inevitable. \par \par \uc2  "The possibility of Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has always been the risk for dollar/yen. The market is bouncing around with some speculation there could be a delay in the start of a war," said Jim McCormick, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  research at Lehman Brothers. \par \par \uc2  "But the delay could be actually a worst case scenario for the dollar because it will prolong the Iraq situation while the probability of war is not changed." \par \par \uc2  By 1055 GMT the dollar stood at 116.92 yen, having set a seven-month low last week of 116.34. Against the euro it stood at $1.1065, within striking distance of Monday's four-year low of $1.1067. \par \par \uc2  The United States and Britain said the vote had been delayed after France and Russia threatened to veto the move and six swing nations on the U.N. Security Council remained uncommitted. \par \par \uc2  The Security Council begins an open debate on the crisis later on Tuesday and diplomats say the U.S. and Britain are prepared to put back a resolution vote possibly until Thursday or later. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  THREAT \par \par \uc2  The dollar managed to hold above 117 yen as speculation grew \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which has admitted covert \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  several times in January and February, might step up its campaign against the yen's strength. \par \par \uc2  Japanese officials worry that excessive strength in the yen could hurt exports, seen as the main support for a faltering economic recovery. \par \par \uc2  Investors grew deeply worried as Tokyo stocks fell below the 8,000 mark for the first time since 1983 on Monday, just before the March 30 fiscal year-end book closing for most Japanese companies. \par \par \uc2  No officials confirmed the Nikkei report on government plans but Finance Minister Masajuro Shiokawa did say \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  immediately in the \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  market if they saw undesirable volatility. \par \par \uc2  "Theoretically, if the authorities want to stop the yen's appreciation, they can sell yen as much as they want. There's no limit," said Kota Kimura, assistant manager at Shinkin \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  WAR AND ECONOMIC IMPACT \par \par \uc2  Still, the dollar's health is still tied to developments concerning Iraq, with all eyes on Washington's attempt to enlist the help of other United Nations' members to disarm Iraq by force if necessary. \par \par \uc2  Diplomats at the U.N. said on Monday the six undecided members of the Security Council had weighed delaying a deadline for Iraqi compliance to April 17, a month later than demanded in a U.S.-British-Spanish draft resolution. \par \par \uc2  Analysts are concerned that the economic impact of waging a war with limited financial support from a smaller coalition of nations would exacerbate the weakness of the U.S. economy, the stock market and the dollar. \par \par \uc2  "It's not just that a war may be about to begin but also that there is growing concern about the U.S. economy even if the war ends swiftly," said Kosuke Hanao, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  sales at Royal Bank of Scotland in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  That may be why speculation is growing the Federal Reserve may cut interest rates by 25 basis points from the current 1.25 percent, when it meets next Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Last time the Fed delivered a surprise 50 basis points, the dollar tumbled across the board as the rate cut reduced the cost of hedging investor dollar exposure. \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere, German industrial output jumped by 1.6 percent month on month in January, beating expectations and reversing a sharp decline in December. \par \par \uc2  U.S. Treasury Secretary John Snow will give a speech on economic initiatives in Washington later at 1430 GMT. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030311dz3b00lrs\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
