\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar teeters above lows, Japan  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  threat helps. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Christina Fincher \par \uc2 648 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2003\par 09:49\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, March 11 (Reuters) - The dollar held above last week's seven-month low against the yen on Tuesday as a report that Japan may beef up its campaign for a weaker \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  helped offset pressure on the greenback from Iraqi war fears. \par \par \uc2  The Nihon Keizai Shimbun business daily reported the government and Bank of Japan were prepared to steady the domestic stock market by introducing measures that could include massive yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  Still, expectations that Washington will soon wage war on Iraq, and concerns - sparked by poor U.S. job data last week - that U.S. recovery was far from assured kept the dollar mired within half a cent of recent four-year lows at $1.1067 per euro \par \par \uc2  "The newspaper report of overt and aggressive yen selling by Japan is being believed by the market and this is giving the dollar some support," said Mitul Kotecha, global head of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  research at Credit Agricole Indosuez. \par \par \uc2  "The fact that no vote will take place at the U.N. today has also eased immediate pressure." \par \par \uc2  The United States and Britain originally set Tuesday as the target date for a vote on a second resolution giving Iraq until March 17 to satisfy all members that it was fully cooperating with U.N. disarmament demands. \par \par \uc2  Officials from both countries confirmed such a vote had been delayed after France and Russia threatened to veto the move and six swing nations on the U.N. Security Council remained uncommitted. \par \par \uc2  MASSIVE \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2 ? \par \par \uc2  The dollar was up a quarter percent at 117.15 yen as U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bears were held in check by speculation that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which has admitted covert \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  several times in January and February, might step up its effort to curb the yen's strength. \par \par \uc2  Japanese officials worry that excessive strength in the yen could hurt exports, seen as the main support for a faltering economic recovery. \par \par \uc2  Traders think the government is deeply worried about the health of the Tokyo stock market. The Nikkei share average fell below the 8,000 mark for the first time since 1983 on Monday - just three weeks before the end-March book-closing for most Japanese companies. \par \par \uc2  The Nihon Keizai Shimbun reported that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Finance Ministry is considering massive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  of about 1.0 trillion yen ($8.56 billion) a day - substantially bigger than \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  so far. \par \par \uc2  "Theoretically, if the authorities want to stop the yen's appreciation, they can sell yen as much as they want. There's no limit," said Kota Kimura, assistant manager at Shinkin \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Whether massive or not, traders think \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  could \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  any time the dollar hovers below 117 yen, with 115 yen seen as the most important level for Japan to protect. \par \par \uc2  NEW DEADLINE? \par \par \uc2  Still, the dollar's health is still tied to developments concerning Iraq, with all eyes on Washington's attempt to enlist the help of other United Nations' members to disarm Iraq, by force if necessary. \par \par \uc2  Diplomats at the U.N. said on Monday the six undecided members of the Security Council had weighed delaying a deadline for Iraqi compliance to April 17, a month later than demanded in a U.S.-British-Spanish draft resolution. \par \par \uc2  Analysts say that concerns about the economic impact of waging a war with limited financial support from a smaller coalition of nations - as well as the possibility of new terror attacks on U.S. soil - would exacerbate the weakness of the U.S. economy, the stock market and the dollar. \par \par \uc2  "It's not just that a war may be about to begin but also that there is growing concern about the U.S. economy even if the war ends swiftly," said Kosuke Hanao, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  sales at Royal Bank of Scotland in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030311dz3b00gzb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
