\par\par \b \uc2  UPDATE 2-Outgoing BOJ chief takes issue with  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  policy. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Ritsuko Ando \par \uc2 742 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2003\par 11:07\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, March 7 (Reuters) - Outgoing Bank of Japan Governor Masaru Hayami took a swipe at the government on Friday over its new \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  tactics, saying it was breaching an international protocol by \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  covertly in large amounts. \par \par \uc2  Less than two weeks before ending his five-year term - during which he was under constant pressure from the government to further ease the BOJ's unprecedentedly loose policy - Hayami took issue with attempts to reign in the yen's export-crimping strength. \par \par \uc2  In \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  acts merely as an agent to execute orders from the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which has the control over the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy. \par \par \uc2  Hayami said any attempt to manipulate \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were either futile or against international agreements - a remark flying directly in the face of the MOF, which last week disclosed that it had discretely sold yen for dollars and euros in February. \par \par \uc2  "It is difficult to change \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  levels unless \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is done in significant amounts," Hayami told a regular news conference. "The market is open 24 hours a day. You can move it a bit but not for long." \par \par \uc2  Hayami went on to say that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  should not "\b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in large amounts covertly", saying it went against an agreement among members of the International Monetary Fund. \par \par \uc2  The MOF confirmed last week that the authorities had conducted \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the second straight month in February to stem the yen's rise, spending more than 500 billion yen ($4.26 billion) to buy dollars and euros. \par \par \uc2  Breaking with the practice in recent years, the MOF did not immediately confirm \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in January and February, only disclosing the actions after the BOJ's monthly data already revealed it had stepped in. \par \par \uc2  Within hours of Hayami's comments, traders said Japanese authorities were selling the yen again as the dollar fell toward the 117 yen level, within whisker of six-month lows around 116.85 set earlier this week, amid jitters over a possible war in Iraq. \par \par \uc2  DIVERGENT STANCES \par \par \uc2  Hayami said weakening the yen would hurt the economies of its neighbours and that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  must not attempt any large-scale \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  without the agreement of these countries. \par \par \uc2  But the government has been keen to prevent a runaway rise in the yen as it would dampen exports, one of the few bright spots in its ailing economy. \par \par \uc2  Hiroshi Watanabe, the head of the MOF's international bureau, told reporters on Thursday that the authorities were trying to protect "real" interest in the market, or commercial flows, even if that meant tougher life for speculators. \par \par \uc2  "It is undesirable to have movements that adversely affect those who have real demand for \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Watanabe said. \par \par \uc2  "But if there are those who find it difficult to make a killing in the market (by speculative trades), it is fine for us that they do not come into the market." \par \par \uc2  Hayami, who as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief is the guardian of the nation's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , is known to be a proponent of a strong yen. \par \par \uc2  He reiterated his view that the value of a country's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is a reflection of its economic strength and that the government should not seek to weaken it. \par \par \uc2  Traders say Hayami's comments came as no surprise and would have no effect on the MOF's \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy. \par \par \uc2  "He is just stating his well known personal view and I don't think there is any particular significance in terms of actual policy," said Junya Tanase, global markets officer at J.P. Morgan Chase in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  Hayami - who turns 78 later this month and cuts a slight, hunched-back figure - departs amid widespread criticism that he failed to halt a fall in prices and give Japan's ailing economy the necessary support. \par \par \uc2  During his term, Tokyo's main stock average lost around half its value and the economy lurched into its worst postwar downturn as deflation weighed on growth and exacerbated the banking sector's bad loan problem. \par \par \uc2  Hayami argued against critics who said he failed to do enough for the economy during his term. \par \par \uc2  "We have always been the first to act," he said, reiterating his insistence that there was a limit to what monetary policy alone could achieve and that the government had to try harder to reform a banking system paralysed by bad loans. ($1=117.32 yen). \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030307dz3700fwo\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
