\par\par \b \uc2  POLL-Weak outlook,  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  seen pushing yen down. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Carolyn Cohn \par \uc2 640 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2003\par 12:02\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, March 6 (Reuters) - A weak Japanese economic outlook coupled with \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stop the yen from strengthening is likely to push the yen slightly lower versus the dollar over the coming year, according to a Reuters poll published on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  This month's poll of 50 analysts and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategists, carried out March 4-5, gave a mid-range forecast for the yen at 118 per dollar in one month's time. \par \par \uc2  Analysts then saw the yen at 120 per dollar in three months, 121 in six months and 120 per dollar in 12 months. The forecasts were for a stronger yen than in last month's poll. \par \par \uc2  Forecasts for the yen varied from 114 to 125 per dollar on a one-month horizon, and from 108 to 140 on a 12-month basis. \par \par \uc2  The yen was trading around 117 per dollar on Thursday, as recent news of covert yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Japanese authorities in January and February failed to stem dollar selling on fears of a U.S.-led war against Iraq. \par \par \uc2  The yen hit six-month highs of 116.80 per dollar last week. \par \par \uc2  "Perceived risk that the U.S. may have to go it alone in Iraq, comments by U.S. Treasury Secretary John Snow that he is unconcerned over present dollar weakness, and traditional early-to-mid March fiscal year-end repatriation flows are putting strong downward pressure on dollar/yen," said David Mozina at Bank of America. \par \par \uc2  "Arrayed against that trend are the valiant war-room staffers of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 's International Bureau watching flows and the yen's every move around the clock, ready to pounce if \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  red lines are crossed." \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  confirmed last week it had conducted \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in February, buying dollars and euros worth about 513 billion yen. It said the euro-buying had been "far less" than dollar-buying against the yen. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  also \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in covert \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  in January, spending a little less than 700 billion yen to buy dollars. \par \par \uc2  GLOOMY TIMES \par \par \uc2  Japanese authorities are fighting to cap the strength of the yen, which threatens to damage the country's fragile export-led recovery. Their repeated attempts have so far prevented the yen from rising beyond 115. \par \par \uc2  Analysts say the yen strength is unwarranted by domestic fundamentals, with the Bank of Japan maintaining its sombre view of the economy on Thursday for a fourth straight month, saying business conditions were unlikely to recover for some time. \par \par \uc2  "Risk aversion should help the yen in the short run, but the bad combination of slow growth and deflation in Japan will send the exchange rate lower in the second part of the year," said Asmara Jamaleh, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  economist at Banca Intesa. \par \par \uc2  But the choice of Toshihiko Fukui to replace outgoing BOJ governor Masaru Hayami is likely to put a floor under yen losses, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  Fukui is not expected to depart radically from the BOJ's current stance, while other candidates for the post were regarded as more likely to introduce yen-depressing measures to boost inflation. "The appointment of Fukui, the more conventional candidate for BOJ governor, is likely to frustrate the more bearish views on the yen," said Peter Luxton at MMS International. \par \par \uc2  Implicit cross rates from the poll showed euro/yen at 129.32 in one month, 129.47 in three months, 130.08 in six months and 131.25 in twelve months, according to the mid-range forecasts. \par \par \uc2  The euro has been on a roll against the yen in recent weeks, in a spillover from safe-haven euro gains against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  The euro was trading at around 128.50 yen on Thursday. The single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hit a 3-1/2 year high of 130.81 last month. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030306dz3600lx7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw200\pich25\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3000\pichgoal375
