\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar Nears 4-Year Low Against Euro Before Rally \b0\par\par\uc2 879 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2003\par 00:23\par \uc2  Dow Jones Business News \par \uc2 DJON\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2003, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par A Wall Street Journal Online News Roundup\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par NEW YORK -- The dollar ended modestly higher against the euro after\par slipping briefly into new, lower ranges that approached a four-year low\par against Europe's common \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , amid faltering confidence about the\par U.S. economic rebound and a sense that a war could be just around the\par corner.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  The euro's intraday gains were the most striking feature of the session and may herald an assault on the $1.10 mark in the next few days, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategists said. Meanwhile, the greenback was clearly higher against the yen due to persistent fears of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Late Tuesday afternoon in New York, the dollar was trading at &#165;117.90, up from &#165;117.58 late Monday in New York. The euro was trading at $1.0878, off its global session highs of $1.0933 and modestly down from $1.0889 late Monday. Against the Swiss franc, the dollar was at 1.3400 francs, modestly up from 1.3382 francs late Monday. Sterling was at $1.5809, up from $1.5782. \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere in North America, Canada's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  raised interest rates in a response to the robust domestic economy, proving very much an exception to major global central banks' current tendency to ease. \par \par \uc2  In addition to raising benchmark overnight interest rates by a quarter-percentage point to 3.0%, the Bank of Canada also issued a remarkably detailed and explicit statement of its policy decision that bolstered expectations the bank will continue raising interest rates, possibly boosting the overnight rate by as much as another percentage point by the end of the year. \par \par \uc2  "[The] level of economic activity in Canada remains near full production capacity. In these circumstances, the persistence of above-target rates of inflation has elevated the risk of an increase in inflation expectations," the BOC said in a statement. \par \par \uc2  The timing of further increases is the only unknown element, with the bank's statement listing a number of factors that will determine the pace of tightening, including the impact on confidence of geopolitical and global economic uncertainties. \par \par \uc2  Growing fears that the U.S. and a small group of allies may shortly attack Iraq, probably without the backing of the United Nations, and some capital flows data suggesting waning foreign appetite for U.S. assets are also conspiring to push the dollar lower. \par \par \uc2  Yet above all, the euro's most recent push higher, aided by stronger-than-expected retail sales data from Germany, has been driven by a dawning realization that the U.S. economic rebound is flailing. \par \par \uc2  "Signs in December and January that things were improving from the "soft spot" [the U.S. economy had waded through] have faded," said Robert Sinche, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist with Citibank in New York. "There are renewed concerns about U.S. growth going forward that are behind the move," lower of the dollar, he added. \par \par \uc2  Adding to the prevailing gloomy undertone, Federal Reserve Bank of Atlanta President Jack Guynn said Tuesday that higher energy prices are a hindrance to the economy's recovery, while Fed Chairman Alan Greenspan warned that housing prices may slip. \par \par \uc2  Mr. Sinche cited "a mosaic of weaker U.S. data" for February, including the softer-than-expected Institute for Supply Management manufacturing report released Monday, a decline in auto sales, and rising weekly claims for unemployment insurance. \par \par \uc2  At the same time, the latest capital flows data -- for the month of December -- from the Treasury Department have pointed to declining demand among some groups of foreign investors for U.S. Treasury bonds. \par \par \uc2  The Bush administration's latest statements about Iraq kept traders on their toes, making for some very choppy trading Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  A few hours after he said that the U.S. will press for a vote on a new U.N. resolution against Iraq, White House spokesman Ari Fleischer backed away from that position, saying he couldn't foresee all possibilities. \par \par \uc2  Secretary of State Colin Powell then said the U.S. will decide early next week whether to seek a Security Council vote on approving a war against Iraq, as financial market investors brooded on the problems the U.S. is facing in gathering broad support for any such campaign. \par \par \uc2  The dollar is suffering "further slippage from developments in Iraq," with sentiment worsening on the sense of growing "isolation that the U.S. is falling into and as a follow-on from global equity markets," many of which declined Tuesday, said David Mozina, head of G10 strategy with Banc of America Securities in New York. \par \par \uc2  Traders remained nervous about bidding the dollar lower against the yen amid persistent worries that the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  might be prepared to covertly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in order to weaken the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategists in New York and London said Tuesday that although they hadn't seen \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , they suspected the BOJ was at work pushing third parties to sell yen in the overlap between the Asian and European trading sessions. \par \par \uc2  -- Don Curren in Toronto contributed to this report. \par \par \uc2  Write to John Parry at john.parry@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  Copyright (c) 2003 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2  All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires \par \par \uc2  03-04-03 1823ET \par \par \uc2 Dokument djon000020030304dz3400a6p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
