\par\par \b \uc2  UPDATE 1-BOJ  \highlight22\uc2 intervenes \highlight\uc2  to buy dollars for yen-bankers. \b0\par\par\uc2 315 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2003\par 03:51\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, March 4 (Reuters) - Japanese monetary authorities are believed to have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Tuesday, buying dollars for yen, market sources said. \par \par \uc2  The sources said the Bank of Japan, acting as an agent for the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MOF), was believed to have been buying dollars at around 117.50/55 yen \par \par \uc2  A senior MOF official declined to comment. \par \par \uc2  Last Friday, \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  confirmed that it had conducted \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in February for the second straight month. BOJ data showed \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  spent about 513 billion yen ($4.36 billion) in \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in February compared with 678 billion yen in January. \par \par \uc2  Japanese officials fear excessive yen strength could undermine exports, a pillar of the nation's faltering economic recovery. \par \par \uc2  MOF officials have said they will continue to monitor movements in the market and act as necessary. \par \par \uc2  Dealers had said they had detected the BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  since late February as the dollar dropped below 119 yen. \par \par \uc2  As of 0237 GMT, the dollar stood at 117.63 yen against 117.53 in late Monday U.S. trade. It dipped to a low of 117.45 yen earlier in Tokyo trade. \par \par \uc2  On Thursday, the greenback dropped to 116.85 yen, its lowest in nearly six months, on growing nervousness over a looming war in Iraq and signs of weakness in the U.S. economy. \par \par \uc2  That was down about four percent from this year's high of 121.78 yen hit about two weeks ago. \par \par \uc2  Japan has been selling its own \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  since 1999 and the latest \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  will increase Japanese external reserves, which were already at a record high of $478.593 billion at the end of January, more than twice as high as in January 1999. \par \par \uc2  During the period between 1999 and 2002, Japan sold the yen against the dollar and the euro on 32 days. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030304dz340053i\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw200\pich25\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3000\pichgoal375
